cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these colourings, please cite this work and the papers it builds on (Cremer 2026; Kuznetsov 2016; Radziszowski, DS1 rev. 18)."
title: "R(8,10) >= 346: a colouring of K_345 with no red K_8 and no blue K_10"
abstract: >-
  We give a colouring of the edges of K_345 containing no red K_8 and no blue K_10,
  which proves R(8,10) >= 346. The previous bound, R(8,10) >= 345, is due to Cremer
  (2026), who improved the value 343 recorded in revision 18 of Radziszowski's dynamic
  survey. Our colouring is obtained by the same device, applied once more: add one
  vertex to Cremer's colouring of K_344 and repair the monochromatic cliques that
  appear.
authors:
